hadiths[64]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27331","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freed slave woman of Maymuna, and said: Why did they not take its hide and tan it and benefit from it? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is dead meat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only eating it is forbidden. Sufyan said: This phrase I heard only from al-Zuhri: Eating it is forbidden. My father said: Sufyan said it twice: From Maymuna."
"27332","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, that a mouse fell into clarified butter and died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, he said: Take it and what is around it and throw it away, and eat it."
"27333","Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Shatha Jabir, meaning Ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, she said: I used to bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from a single vessel."
"27334","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna bint al-Harith, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed from major impurity, he would begin by washing his hands, then pour with his right over his left and wash his private part, then strike his hand on the ground and wipe it, then wash it, then perform his ablution for prayer, then pour over his head and over the rest of his body, then move aside and wash his feet."
"27335","Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, Abdullah said: And Abu al-Rabi narrated to me, he said: Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"27336","Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsa narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Sabbaq, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up gloomy, so it was said to him: What is wrong with you, O Messenger of Allah, you woke up gloomy? He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, promised to meet me but did not meet me, and he never broke his promise to me. He did not come to him that night, nor the second, nor the third. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) suspected a puppy, and it was under our low table, so he ordered it and it was taken out. Then he took water and sprinkled its place. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came and said: You promised me but I did not see you. He said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image. So he ordered on that day the killing of dogs, he said: Until permission was sought even for the small dog of the garden wall, and he would order it to be killed."
"27337","Sulayman ibn Dawud Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution with the leftover of her bath from major impurity."
"27338","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became in major impurity, so I bathed from a large bowl, and some leftover remained. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to bathe from it, so I said: I have already bathed from it. He said: Water is not affected by major impurity, or nothing makes it impure. So he bathed from it."
"27339","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ruling concerning a mouse that fell into solid clarified butter of theirs. He said: Throw it and what is around it away, and eat your clarified butter."
"27340","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Maymuna, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed wearing a woolen cloak belonging to one of his wives, with part of it over her. Sufyan said: I think he said: While she was menstruating."
"27341","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Maymuna bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a small mat."
"27342","Bakr ibn Isa al-Rasibi narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had narrated to us, he said: I heard my maternal aunt Maymuna bint al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she would be menstruating while lying beside the place of prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he prayed on his small mat; when he prostrated, the edge of his garment would touch me."
"27343","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Sulayman al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Shaddad narrated to us, he said: I heard Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand and pray at night while I was sleeping beside him; when he prostrated, his clothes would touch me while I was menstruating."
"27344","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the small mat, then prostrate, and his garment would touch me while I was beside him and I was menstruating."
"27345","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn al-Asamm, my father said: And it was read to Sufyan: His name is Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, the son of the brother of Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from his uncle, from Maymuna, and she is his maternal aunt, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, and there was a lamb that wanted to pass in front of him, he would spread himself out."
"27346","Sufyan narrated to us, from Manbudh, from his mother, she said: I was with Maymuna, and Ibn Abbas came to her and said: O my son, why is your head disheveled? He said: Umm Ammar, my hairdresser, is menstruating. She said: O my son, what has menstruation to do with the hand? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter upon one of us while she was menstruating, and place his head in her lap and recite the Quran while she was menstruating. Then one of us would stand with his small mat and place it in the mosque while she was menstruating. O my son, what has menstruation to do with the hand?"
"27347","Sufyan narrated to us, from Manbudh, from his mother, she heard it from Maymuna, she said: One of us would spread the small mat for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while she was menstruating, then he would pray upon it."
"27348","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abu Bakkar, he said: I prayed behind Abu al-Malih over a funeral, and he said: Straighten your rows and make your intercession good, and if I were to choose a man I would choose him. Then he said: Abd Allah ibn Salit narrated to me, my father said: And Abu Ubayda al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salit narrated to me, from one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Maymuna, and he was her brother through breastfeeding, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim over whom a community prays except that they will be intercessors for him. And Abu al-Malih said: The community is forty to a hundred and more."
"27349","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us, and Ali ibn Ishaq informed us, Abd Allah informed us, he said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, he said: Bukayr narrated to me that Kurayb, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, narrated to him that he heard Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from a shoulder, then stood and prayed without performing ablution."
"27350","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, and Ibn Shihab narrated, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Ibn Abbas, that he informed him that Khalid ibn al-Walid entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Maymuna bint al-Harith while she was menstruating, and there was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the meat of a mastigure brought by Umm Hufayd bint al-Harith from Najd, and she was under a man from Banu Jafar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not eat anything until he knew what it was. So some of the women said: Will you not inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he is eating? So she informed him that it is the meat of a mastigure, so he left it. Khalid said: So I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is it forbidden? He said: No, but it is a food not found among my people, so I find myself disliking it. Khalid said: So I pulled it toward me and ate it, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking."
"27351","He said: And al-Asamm narrated to him, from Maymuna, and he was in her care, meaning this hadith, and I think that al-Asamm is Yazid ibn al-Asamm."
"27352","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Habib, meaning Ibn al-Shahid, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me while we were in a state of halal, after we returned from Mecca."
"27353","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Mansur, he thought it from Salim, from Maymuna, that she took a loan, so it was said to her: You borrow while you have no means to repay it? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no one who borrows a loan, with Allah knowing that he intends to repay it, except that He will repay it for him."
"27354","Yala narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I freed a slave girl of mine, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and I informed him of her freeing. He said: May Allah reward you. Had you given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward."
"27355","Waki narrated to us, Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, he would spread himself out until one behind him could see the whiteness of his armpits."
"27356","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Budayya, she said: Maymuna bint al-Harith sent me to the wife of Abd Allah ibn Abbas, and there was kinship between them, and I saw her bed separated from his bed, so I thought that was due to desertion, so I asked her and she said: No, but I am menstruating, and when I menstruate he does not come near my bed. So I came to Maymuna and mentioned that to her, so she sent me back to Ibn Abbas and said: Is it aversion to the Sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sleep with a menstruating woman among his wives, with nothing between them except a garment not going beyond the knees."
"27357","Hajjaj and Abu Kamil narrated to us, they said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Habib the freed slave of Urwa, from Budayya, and he mentioned the hadith."
"27358","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Muawiya ibn Salih narrated to us, from Azhar ibn Said, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Saib, the son of the brother of Maymuna al-Hilaliyya, that he narrated to him that Maymuna said to him: O son of my brother, shall I not charm you with the charm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes. She said: In the name of Allah I charm you, and Allah will heal you from every ailment in you: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind, and heal, You are the Healer, there is no healer but You."
"27359","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, he said: Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj narrated to me, from Kurayb the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, that he said: I heard Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I freed a slave girl during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I mentioned that to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Had you given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward."
"27360","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Amir narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, meaning Ibn Aqil, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, and Ata ibn Yasar, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Do not make nabidh in gourds, nor in pitch-coated vessels, nor in hantam, nor in naqir. Abd al-Rahman said: Nor in jars. And every intoxicant is forbidden."
"27361","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gourds, naqir, jars, and pitch-coated vessels, and said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"27362","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from al-Qasim, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"27363","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Mabad ibn Abbas, that he said: A woman complained of an ailment and said: If Allah heals me, I will go out and pray in Bayt al-Maqdis. So she recovered, and she prepared to go out. Then she came to Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to greet her, and informed her of that. She said: Sit and eat what I have made, and pray in the mosque of the Messenger, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in it is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques except the mosque of the Kaba."
"27364","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to us, he said: I read in a book of Ata ibn Yasar, with Ata ibn Yasar, he said: I asked Maymuna the wife of the Prophet about wiping over the leather socks. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, does a person wipe over the leather socks every time without taking them off? He said: Yes."
"27365","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Fazara narrating from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while in halal and consummated the marriage with her while in halal, and she died at Sarif, and he buried her in the shade where he had consummated with her. So we descended into her grave, I and Ibn Abbas."
"27366","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Aws narrated to us, from Bilal al-Absi, from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: How will you be when religion becomes confused, desire appears, brothers differ, and the Ancient House is burned?"
"27367","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Labiba ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Rafi, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My nation will remain in good as long as children of adultery do not spread among them; when children of adultery spread among them, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is about to encompass them with punishment."
"27368","Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Jafar narrated to us, and Ali ibn Thabit said: Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, he said: Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Asamm, narrated to us, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, he would spread his arms until one behind him could see the brightness of his armpits."
"27369","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, he said: Hanzala narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed two rakas before Asr, so he prayed them afterwards."
"27370","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Rushdin ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me that Kathir ibn Farqad narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Malik ibn Hudhafa narrated to him, from his mother al-Aliya bint Sumay or Subay, the doubt is from Abd Allah, that Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by men of Quraysh dragging a sheep of theirs like a donkey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Had you taken its hide. They said: It is dead meat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water and qaraz purify it."
"27371","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Manbudh informed me that his mother informed him that while she was sitting with Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Ibn Abbas entered upon her and said: Why are you disheveled? He said: Umm Ammar, my hairdresser, is menstruating. She said: O my son, what has menstruation to do with the hand? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter upon one of us while she was reclining and menstruating, knowing that she was menstruating, and recline upon her and recite the Quran while reclining upon her, or enter upon her while she was sitting and menstruating, and recline in her lap and recite the Quran in her lap. And she, while menstruating, would stand and spread for him the small mat in his place of prayer, and Ibn Bakr said: His small mat, so he would pray upon it in my house. O my son, what has menstruation to do with the hand?"
"27372","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Nafi the freed slave of Ibn Umar say: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Mabad narrated to us that Ibn Abbas narrated that Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the mosque of the Kaba."
"27373","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah informed us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: I heard Nafi say: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Mabad ibn Abbas narrated to us that Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the like of it."
"27374","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Mabad ibn Abbas, that Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in it is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among the mosques except the mosque of the Kaba."
"27375","Abu Ubayda Abd al-Wahid al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Farrukh Abu Bakkar narrated to us that Abu al-Malih went out for a funeral, and when he stood straight they thought he would say the takbir, so he turned and said: Stand straight so your intercession may be good, for if I were to choose a man I would choose this one, except that Abd Allah ibn Salit narrated to me, from one of the Mothers of the Believers, namely Maymuna, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim over whom a community of people prays except that they will be intercessors for him. He said: So I asked Abu al-Malih about the community, and he said: Forty."
"27376","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Hanzala narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal narrated to us, he said: Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan led us in Asr prayer, then he sent to Maymuna, then he followed it with another man. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preparing an expedition and had no mounts with him, then mounts came to him from charity, and he began dividing them among them, but they detained him until Asr became urgent. He used to pray two rakas before Asr, or whatever Allah willed, so he prayed Asr, then returned and prayed what he used to pray before it. And when he prayed a prayer or did something, he liked to persist in it."
"27377","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from a man, from Maymuna bint al-Harith, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever borrows a loan, with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knowing from him that he intends to repay it, Allah will repay it on his behalf."
"27378","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Yazid al-Asamm, the son of the sister of Maymuna, that she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while they were both in halal at Sarif, after he returned."
"27379","Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Salim, from Kurayb, he said: Ibn Abbas narrated to us, from his maternal aunt Maymuna, she said: I placed washing water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he bathed from major impurity, then I brought him a garment when he bathed, and he said with his hand like this, meaning he refused it."
"27380","Waki narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Salim, from Kurayb, he said: Ibn Abbas narrated to us, from his maternal aunt Maymuna, she said: I placed washing water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he bathed from major impurity, and he tilted the vessel with his left over his right and washed his palms three times, then put his hand in the vessel and poured over his private part, then rubbed his hand on the wall or the ground, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times, and washed his face three times and his forearms three times each, then poured over his head three times, then poured water over the rest of his body, then moved aside and washed his feet."
"27381","Waki narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymuna, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, he would spread himself out until one behind him could see the whiteness of his armpits."
"27382","Waki narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Amash, he said: I think Abu Khalid al-Walibi mentioned it, from Maymuna bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, while the believer eats in one intestine."
"27383","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Shaybani, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Maymuna, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch her while she was menstruating above the waist-wrapper."
"27384","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into clarified butter. He said: Take it and what is around it and throw it away."
"27385","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shuba, he said: al-Hakam narrated to me, he said: I asked Miqsam, he said: I said: I pray witr with three then go out to prayer fearing it will escape me. He said: It is not proper except with five or seven. So I informed Mujahid and Yahya ibn al-Jazzar of his saying, and they said to me: Ask him from whom. So I asked him, and he said: From the trustworthy one, from Maymuna and Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27386","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from his maternal aunt Maymuna, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to pray on the small mat."
"27387","Hajjaj and Abu Kamil narrated to us, they said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Habib the freed slave of Urwa, from Budayya the freed slave woman of Maymuna, from Maymuna the wife of the Prophet, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch a woman among his wives while she was menstruating if she had a waist-wrapper reaching half the thighs or the knees, wrapped with it."
"27388","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Maymuna bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the small mat."
"27389","Abd al-Razzaq and Yazid narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata said, Ibn Abbas said: Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that a sheep died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not tan its hide and enjoy it?"
"27390","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Budayya the freed slave woman of Maymuna, from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch a menstruating woman among his wives, with a cloth over her up to the knees or up to half the thighs."
"27391","Asbat narrated to us, he said: al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Maymuna, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch his wives above the waist-wrapper while they were menstruating."
"27392","Affan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had narrated to us, he said: I heard Maymuna the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to touch a menstruating woman among his wives, he would order her to wrap herself in a waist-wrapper."
"27393","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymuna bint al-Harith, she said: I placed washing water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and screened him. He poured over his hand and washed it once or twice, Sulayman said: I do not know whether he mentioned the third or not. He said: Then he poured with his right over his left and washed his private part, then rubbed his hand on the ground or the wall, then rinsed his mouth and sniffed water, and washed his face, he said: And washed his head, then poured over his body, then moved aside and washed his feet. She said: So I handed him a cloth, he said: So he said like this and gestured with his hand that I do not want it. Sulayman said: So I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he said: It is so, and he did not deny it. And Ibrahim said: There is no harm in a towel, it is only a habit."
"27394","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Jubayr narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Umar, and he mentioned a hadith, he said: And a man asked him about what may be killed of animals, and he said: One of the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that he ordered the killing of the mouse, the scorpion, the vicious dog, the kite, and the crow."
